<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="57291" href="schedule/2019/spring/MACS/275/57291.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120191" href="schedule/2019/spring.xml">Spring 2019</term><subject id="MACS" href="schedule/2019/spring/MACS.xml">Media and Cinema Studies</subject><course id="275" href="schedule/2019/spring/MACS/275.xml">Am Indian and Indigenous Film</course></parents><sectionNumber>CHP</sectionNumber><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>The topic for this course is 'Sex on the Beach' and will focus on films the Pacific Islands. Have you ever noticed that films set in the Pacific are always about romance or tragedy? This course samples the body of films set in the Pacific Islands to develop our critical visual literacy skills through which we can understand a broader, ongoing, history of Euro American fears and desires as projected through exotic and erotic films of romance and tragedy set in the islands.</sectionText><sectionCappArea>Restricted to Chancellor's Scholar-CHPHonors students.</sectionCappArea><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-01-14Z</startDate><endDate>2019-05-01Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>11:00 AM</start><end>12:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>301</roomNumber><buildingName>Architecture Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Gilbert" firstName="M">Gilbert, M</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>